{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{# Specific context for the main narrative of Section 9 (Attack Vectors/Complexity) #}
{% set output_format_description = "a coherent narrative paragraph (or potentially two short paragraphs) summarizing the analysis of overall attack vector and complexity distributions, suitable for the main body text. Use Markdown for clarity (e.g., simple bolding) if helpful." %}

{% block task_instructions %}
Synthesize the provided chart insights, callouts, and data summaries for "{{ section_title }}" into a flowing narrative text focused on the overall attack vector and complexity landscape.
Your narrative should cover:
1. The dominant attack vectors observed across all vulnerabilities analyzed during the period.
2. The overall distribution between Low and High attack complexity and its implications.
3. Any potential relationship or notable points arising from considering both vector and complexity together.
Integrate the key points highlighted in the callouts. Aim for 3-6 sentences. You may use simple Markdown (like **bold**) for emphasis if appropriate.
{% endblock task_instructions %}

{% block data_context %}
Section Key: {{ data_context_payload.section_key | default('section_9_attack_vector_deep_dive') }}

Chart Insights Generated for this Section:
{% for chart_id, insight in data_context_payload.chart_insights_in_section.items() %}
- Insight ({{ chart_id }}): {{ insight }}
{% else %}
- No specific chart insights provided.
{% endfor %}

Callouts Generated for this Section:
{% for callout_key, callout_text in data_context_payload.callouts_in_section.items() %}
- {{ callout_key | replace("_", " ") | title }}: {{ callout_text }}
{% else %}
- No callouts generated for this section.
{% endfor %}

Data Summaries for Charts in this Section:
{% for chart_id, summary in data_context_payload.charts_data_summaries_in_section.items() %}
--- Data Summary: {{ chart_id }} ---
{{ summary }}
--- End Summary ---
{% else %}
- No chart data summaries provided.
{% endfor %}
{% endblock data_context %}
